# Payments rules

- Define a Vimla `PaymentProvider` abstraction; do not couple domain logic to T-Kassa, CloudPayments, YooKassa or another processor.
- Start development with a `MockPaymentProvider` before real acquiring.
- Activate a plan/top-up only after verified provider confirmation/webhook, never from browser redirect alone.
- Verify webhook signatures/authenticity according to the selected provider.
- Store provider event/payment IDs and enforce uniqueness/idempotency.
- Persist raw provider payload only if needed and safe; redact sensitive payment data.
- Refunds/cancellations must create explicit domain events/ledger adjustments; do not silently mutate history.
- Never store PAN/CVV or other card secrets.
